        "id": "v1",
        "label": "Map render path",
        "focus": ["client", "map_screen", "camera_ctl", "camera_hooks", "mc_client", "voxy", "shader_hooks", "roof_ore", "fog_hooks", "fog_patch", "iris"],
        "note": "The map is a screen over Minecraft's normal world pass: the real camera is moved to the map pose, Voxy draws its cached LODs, and patched Voxy shaders apply the Nether roof cut and the ore mask."
      },
      {
        "id": "v2",
        "label": "Waypoints, sync and map sharing",
        "focus": ["map_screen", "picker", "waypoints", "sync_client", "sync_server", "section_bridge", "voxy", "config_files"],
        "note": "Pins are placed by a voxel ray pick on Voxy data, kept locally or on the self-hosted sync server, and map sharing relays Voxy sections through the same server."
      },
      {
        "id": "v3",
        "label": "HUD, minimap and optional mods",
